		{
			"type": "yaml",
			"value": "title: How Next.js supports AI coding agents\nnav_title: AI Coding Agents\ndescription: Learn how Next.js helps AI coding agents use current framework guidance, inspect applications, verify changes, and report issues."
		},
		{
			"type": "paragraph",
			"children": [
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": "AI coding agents may rely on training data that predates the Next.js version installed in a project. To help agents use current APIs and verify their work, Next.js provides and evaluates version-matched documentation, managed project instructions, agent-guided upgrades, runtime tools, structured errors, reusable Skills, and optional agent feedback. See the results in the "
				},
				{
					"type": "link",
					"title": null,
					"url": "https://nextjs.org/evals",
					"children": [
						{
							"type": "text",
							"value": "Next.js agent evaluations"
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": "."
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"type": "paragraph",
			"children": [
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": "For more background, read about the AI tooling introduced in "
				},
				{
					"type": "link",
					"title": null,
					"url": "/blog/next-16-2-ai",
					"children": [
						{
							"type": "text",
							"value": "Next.js 16.2"
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": " and "
				},
				{
					"type": "link",
					"title": null,
					"url": "/blog/next-16-3-ai-improvements",
					"children": [
						{
							"type": "text",
							"value": "Next.js 16.3"
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": "."
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"type": "html",
			"value": "<span id=\"step-1-point-agents-at-the-bundled-docs\" />"
		},
		{
			"type": "heading",
			"depth": 2,
			"children": [
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": "Version-matched documentation"
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"type": "paragraph",
			"children": [
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": "Next.js 16.2 and later include documentation that matches the installed framework version. The documentation is available at "
				},
				{
					"type": "inlineCode",
					"value": "node_modules/next/dist/docs/"
				},
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": " and mirrors the structure of the "
				},
				{
					"type": "link",
					"title": null,
					"url": "https://nextjs.org/docs",
					"children": [
						{
							"type": "text",
							"value": "Next.js documentation site"
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": ":"
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"type": "code",
			"lang": "txt",
			"meta": null,
			"value": "node_modules/next/dist/docs/\n├── 01-app/\n│   ├── 01-getting-started/\n│   ├── 02-guides/\n│   └── 03-api-reference/\n├── 02-pages/\n├── 03-architecture/\n└── index.mdx"
		},
		{
			"type": "paragraph",
			"children": [
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": "The bundled copy gives coding agents access to the APIs and patterns supported by the project without a network request or external lookup. "
				},
				{
					"type": "link",
					"title": null,
					"url": "../01-getting-started/18-upgrading.md",
					"children": [
						{
							"type": "text",
							"value": "Upgrading Next.js"
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": " also updates the bundled documentation."
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"type": "heading",
			"depth": 3,
			"children": [
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": "Managed documentation instructions"
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"type": "paragraph",
			"children": [
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": "Next.js makes the bundled documentation discoverable through managed instructions in "
				},
				{
					"type": "inlineCode",
					"value": "AGENTS.md"
				},
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": " at the project root. Coding agents such as Claude Code, Codex, Cursor, and GitHub Copilot read this file when they start a session."
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"type": "paragraph",
			"children": [
				{
					"type": "link",
					"title": null,
					"url": "../03-api-reference/06-cli/create-next-app.md",
					"children": [
						{
							"type": "inlineCode",
							"value": "create-next-app"
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": " creates the agent files for new projects. When "
				},
				{
					"type": "inlineCode",
					"value": "next dev"
				},
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": " detects a coding agent, it creates or updates the managed instructions for existing projects. The block directs the agent to the documentation installed with the project:"
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"type": "code",
			"lang": "md",
			"meta": "filename=\"AGENTS.md\"",
			"value": "<!-- BEGIN:nextjs-agent-rules -->\n\n## This is NOT the Next.js you know\n\nThis version has breaking changes — APIs, conventions, and file structure may all differ from your training data. Read the relevant guide in `node_modules/next/dist/docs/` (resolved from this file's directory; in monorepos the `next` package may not be visible from the repo root) before writing any code. Heed deprecation notices.\n\nThis block is written and re-added by `next dev` — verify at `node_modules/next/dist/server/lib/generate-agent-files.js`. Removing it from a diff only re-creates the uncommitted change; committing it with your work keeps the tree clean.\n\n<!-- END:nextjs-agent-rules -->"
		},
		{
			"type": "paragraph",
			"children": [
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": "Next.js updates only the content between the agent rules markers and preserves the rest of "
				},
				{
					"type": "inlineCode",
					"value": "AGENTS.md"
				},
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": "."
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"type": "paragraph",
			"children": [
				{
					"type": "link",
					"title": null,
					"url": "https://vercel.com/blog/agents-md-outperforms-skills-in-our-agent-evals",
					"children": [
						{
							"type": "text",
							"value": "Research comparing "
						},
						{
							"type": "inlineCode",
							"value": "AGENTS.md"
						},
						{
							"type": "text",
							"value": " with knowledge Skills"
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": " found a 100% pass rate with bundled documentation, compared with up to 79% for Skill-based approaches. See the current "
				},
				{
					"type": "link",
					"title": null,
					"url": "https://nextjs.org/evals",
					"children": [
						{
							"type": "text",
							"value": "Next.js agent evaluation results"
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": "."
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"type": "paragraph",
			"children": [
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": "Managed documentation instructions are enabled by default in Next.js 16.3 and later. See the "
				},
				{
					"type": "link",
					"title": null,
					"url": "../03-api-reference/05-config/01-next-config-js/agentRules.md",
					"children": [
						{
							"type": "inlineCode",
							"value": "agentRules"
						},
						{
							"type": "text",
							"value": " API reference"
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": " to configure or disable them."
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"type": "heading",
			"depth": 3,
			"children": [
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": "Version support"
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"type": "paragraph",
			"children": [
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": "Next.js 16.3 and later include bundled documentation and support managed agent instructions. Next.js 16.2 includes the bundled documentation but does not generate instructions automatically."
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"type": "paragraph",
			"children": [
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": "Next.js 16.1 and earlier do not include the bundled documentation. The legacy "
				},
				{
					"type": "inlineCode",
					"value": "agents-md"
				},
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": " command downloads a version-matched copy to "
				},
				{
					"type": "inlineCode",
					"value": ".next-docs/"
				},
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": " and indexes it in "
				},
				{
					"type": "inlineCode",
					"value": "AGENTS.md"
				},
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": ":"
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"type": "code",
			"lang": "bash",
			"meta": null,
			"value": "npx @next/codemod@canary agents-md"
		},
		{
			"type": "heading",
			"depth": 3,
			"children": [
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": "Docs over the network"
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"type": "paragraph",
			"children": [
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": "The Next.js documentation is also available as Markdown over the network for agents that fetch pages instead of reading "
				},
				{
					"type": "inlineCode",
					"value": "node_modules"
				},
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": ". Every page on "
				},
				{
					"type": "link",
					"title": null,
					"url": "https://nextjs.org/docs",
					"children": [
						{
							"type": "text",
							"value": "nextjs.org/docs"
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": " has a plain Markdown version at its "
				},
				{
					"type": "inlineCode",
					"value": ".md"
				},
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": " URL, and clients that send an "
				},
				{
					"type": "inlineCode",
					"value": "Accept: text/markdown"
				},
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": " header receive Markdown. This includes the per-error pages under "
				},
				{
					"type": "inlineCode",
					"value": "/docs/messages"
				},
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": ", which are not bundled."
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"type": "paragraph",
			"children": [
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": "The index at "
				},
				{
					"type": "link",
					"title": null,
					"url": "https://nextjs.org/docs/llms.txt",
					"children": [
						{
							"type": "inlineCode",
							"value": "/docs/llms.txt"
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": " and the single-file "
				},
				{
					"type": "link",
					"title": null,
					"url": "https://nextjs.org/docs/llms-full.txt",
					"children": [
						{
							"type": "inlineCode",
							"value": "/docs/llms-full.txt"
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": " follow the "
				},
				{
					"type": "link",
					"title": null,
					"url": "https://llmstxt.org/",
					"children": [
						{
							"type": "inlineCode",
							"value": "llms.txt"
